Ihecs Bac 3 DECO project

In a communication school, third year project in which we were tasked to develop a brand launch strategy for a fictional product. 
Our designated product is "a game for ultra-thrifty people". 
We decided to go for an app, directly inspired by duolinguo, on which the user gets hooked by being presented with challenges that earn him points. 
The challenges are in our case linked to thriftyness and are to that end ways of spending less while getting more. 
This app was a prototype of the final product and presents its features in a more hands-on approach than slides from a powerpoint. 
Used only during our final examination, it isn't backed by a data management code and hasn't been given access to the internet. This is indeed a prototype, not a finished product.

What it does achieve is to present a product, a brand identification through colors, a tone of voice and visual identity while also proving our ability to code a near-ready functional product. 
Were this prototype asked to be made production ready, only minor data management and networking features would need to be added, making it a true, near-finished product. 

